  ],
  "paragraphs": [
    [
      "The ",
      { "id": "gobernador", "es": "gobernador", "en": "governor" },
      " sends two of our ",
      { "id": "barco", "es": "barcos", "en": "ships" },
      " to the ",
      { "id": "puerto", "es": "puerto", "en": "port" },
      " of Trinidad, on the south ",
      { "id": "costa", "es": "costa", "en": "coast" },
      " of Cuba, to take on supplies. I go with them. I am on land with some of the men when the ",
      { "id": "tormenta", "es": "tormenta", "en": "storm" },
      " comes."
    ],
    [
      "It begins as rain. Then the ",
      { "id": "viento", "es": "viento", "en": "wind" },
      " comes from the ",
      { "id": "norte", "es": "norte", "en": "north" },
      " and does not stop. The ",
      { "id": "mar", "es": "mar", "en": "sea" },
      " rises into the streets. The houses come apart. Seven or eight ",
      { "id": "hombre", "es": "hombres", "en": "men" },
      " hold each other by the arms so the ",
      { "id": "viento", "es": "viento", "en": "wind" },
      " cannot carry us away. We walk like that all night, and the ",
      { "id": "viento", "es": "viento", "en": "wind" },
      " carries other things past us: ",
      { "id": "voz", "es": "voces", "en": "voices" },
      ", the sound of small bells, ",
      { "id": "flauta", "es": "flautas", "en": "flutes" },
      ", drums, ",
      { "id": "instrumento", "es": "instrumentos", "en": "instruments" },
      " I cannot name. There are no ",
      { "id": "instrumento", "es": "instrumentos", "en": "instruments" },
      ". There is no one there. I write it down as I heard it."
    ],
    [
      "In the morning the ",
      { "id": "tormenta", "es": "tormenta", "en": "storm" },
      " is gone and so are the two ",
      { "id": "barco", "es": "barcos", "en": "ships" },
      ". We find a ship's boat in the top of a tree. We find two bodies on the ",
      { "id": "costa", "es": "costa", "en": "coast" },
      ", so broken by the rocks and the ",
      { "id": "mar", "es": "mar", "en": "sea" },
      " that no one can say who they were. Sixty ",
      { "id": "hombre", "es": "hombres", "en": "men" },
      ", twenty ",
      { "id": "caballo", "es": "caballos", "en": "horses" },
      ", and two ",
      { "id": "barco", "es": "barcos", "en": "ships" },
      " are lost, and with them everything they carried."
    ],
    [
      "The ",
      { "id": "gobernador", "es": "gobernador", "en": "governor" },
      " arrives with the other ",
      { "id": "barco", "es": "barcos", "en": "ships" },
      " some days later. He asks me what happened. I tell him what I have written. He listens with his one eye on the ",
      { "id": "mar", "es": "mar", "en": "sea" },
      ". The ",
      { "id": "hombre", "es": "hombres", "en": "men" },
      " are afraid of the ",
      { "id": "mar", "es": "mar", "en": "sea" },
      " now, and they ask him to wait for winter to pass. He agrees. It is a hard thing to see what a ",
      { "id": "tormenta", "es": "tormenta", "en": "storm" },
      " leaves behind. It is a worse thing to sail into the season of them."
    ],
    [
      "We winter at the ",
      { "id": "puerto", "es": "puerto", "en": "port" },
      " of Xagua. I keep the numbers in my book. Sixty ",
      { "id": "hombre", "es": "hombres", "en": "men" },
      ". Twenty ",
      { "id": "caballo", "es": "caballos", "en": "horses" },
      ". Two ",
      { "id": "barco", "es": "barcos", "en": "ships" },
      ". And a sound of ",
      { "id": "voz", "es": "voces", "en": "voices" },
      " and ",
      { "id": "flauta", "es": "flautas", "en": "flutes" },
      " over the water that I cannot enter in any column."
    ]
  ],
